{
  "requirement": "A GitHub Actions CI workflow MUST run, for pull requests and pushes to `main`, these checks: `cargo habeas coverage -- --locked --workspace` under {cite}`requirements.test-coverage.run`, `cargo test --locked --doc --workspace`, `mdbook test`, the autofix controller tests with `node --test .github/scripts/autofix.test.mjs`, and, in a separate job, the Symposium session-start hook smoke test `tests/symposium_hook_smoke.py`. It also builds the book as documentation under {cite}`requirements.index.render_only`, without requiring collected execution reports for rendering. On a push to `main`, only after every check job passes, it deploys the generated `book/` directory to GitHub Pages. The book MUST set `output.html.site-url` to `/habeas-codicem/` for project-site hosting.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The marked test `tests/repository.rs#fn[ci_tests_pull_requests_and_main_then_deploys_the_book_from_main]` covers each obligation in `requirements.integration.ci`.\n\n- **Triggers:** it asserts the `on:` block is exactly `push: branches: [main]` plus `pull_request`.\n- **Checks in `test-and-build`:** it asserts these steps are present, in this order:\n  - `node --test .github/scripts/autofix.test.mjs`\n  - the habeas build\n  - `cargo habeas coverage -- --locked --workspace`\n  - `cargo habeas coverage-check`\n  - `cargo test --locked --doc --workspace`\n  - `mdbook test`\n  - `mdbook build`\n  - the pages artifact upload\n- **Coverage gate:** it parses the YAML and asserts the `coverage-check` step has no `if` and no `continue-on-error`.\n- **Artifact path:** it asserts the uploaded artifact path is `book`, so the generated `book/` directory is what gets deployed.\n- **Hook job:** it asserts a separate `symposium-hook` job runs `python3 tests/symposium_hook_smoke.py`.\n- **Deploy gating:** it asserts the `deploy` job runs only on `push` to `refs/heads/main`. It also asserts `needs: [test-and-build, symposium-hook]`, so deploy waits for every check job. It asserts `actions/deploy-pages@v4`.\n- **Site URL:** it asserts `site-url` is `/habeas-codicem/`. The key sits under `output.habeas.html`, the book's HTML configuration. I confirmed this in `book.toml#table[output.habeas.html]/pair[site-url]`.\n\nThe clause about building the book without requiring collected execution reports describes the behaviour of `habeas mdbook` under `requirements.index.render_only`. That requirement is cited as context, so its tests are not reassessed here. CI itself only has to build the book with `mdbook build`, and the test checks that step.\n\nThe assertions are substring and order checks on the workflow text. A reviewer would accept them as adequate for a configuration requirement like this one. I found no unmarked relevant test and no missing scenario.",
  "references": "a8abf153c89272233a77553f9d744b8b6c5dbba98424eae9956c0f6b77735200",
  "inputs": [
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.integration.ci",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.integration.ci"
      ],
      "text": [
        ":::{req} ci",
        "A GitHub Actions CI workflow MUST run, for pull requests and pushes to `main`, these checks: `cargo habeas coverage -- --locked --workspace` under {cite}`requirements.test-coverage.run`, `cargo test --locked --doc --workspace`, `mdbook test`, the autofix controller tests with `node --test .github/scripts/autofix.test.mjs`, and, in a separate job, the Symposium session-start hook smoke test `tests/symposium_hook_smoke.py`. It also builds the book as documentation under {cite}`requirements.index.render_only`, without requiring collected execution reports for rendering. On a push to `main`, only after every check job passes, it deploys the generated `book/` directory to GitHub Pages. The book MUST set `output.html.site-url` to `/habeas-codicem/` for project-site hosting.",
        ":::"
      ]
    },
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.test-coverage.run",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.test-coverage.run"
      ],
      "text": [
        ":::{req} run",
        "`habeas coverage [-- <nextest arguments>]` MUST run LLVM-instrumented Rust tests",
        "through `cargo nextest run`, forwarding the supplied arguments and preserving",
        "nextest's configured test concurrency, filtering, and retries. With no supplied",
        "arguments it MUST select the workspace.",
        ":::"
      ]
    },
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.index.render_only",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.index.render_only"
      ],
      "text": [
        ":::{req} render_only",
        "`habeas mdbook` reads annotations and stored reviews to render their connections.",
        "It does not audit repository evidence, check review freshness or dependency",
        "hashes, enforce reference coverage, or assess citation and site reviews.",
        "It does not load saved execution measurements, run tests, collect coverage,",
        "or invoke an assessment model. Source-input and stored-record read or parse",
        "failures produce readable rendering diagnostics rather than a repository",
        "validation verdict.",
        ":::"
      ]
    },
